Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (diagonal value should be less than or equal to the number of columns)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 3 (diagonal value should be greater than or equal to the negative number of rows)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ (0 - shape(v_1, 0))
>>
Rule 4 (out tensor dtype must match the input tensor dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (If out tensor is provided, it must have the same shape as the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 6 (If the input tensor has more than 2 dimensions, the out tensor also should have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then ndim(v_2) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 7 (If the input is a batch of matrices (ndim > 2), the out tensor also should have the same batch size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 2] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 8 (diagonal is an integer between -rows and cols, assuming rows and cols exist)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ (0 - shape(v_1, 0)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 9 (If the input tensor is complex, then the out tensor should also be complex)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 then dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10
